CATEGORIES:Part of the line closed
DESCRIPTION:🚧 Part of the line closed\n\nWest Drayton to Slough\nDates 
 as listed by TfL: Thursday 31 December to Sunday 3 January 2027\n\nTfL liv
 e status (Part Closure\, checked 28 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: Thursd
 ay 31 December\, New Years Day 1 January and Saturday 2 January\, no servi
 ce between West Drayton and Reading. Use GWR services between Slough and R
 eading. There will also be no GWR services between Paddington and Slough /
  Greenford\, with some long distance services diverted to/from Euston\, no
 t serving Reading. Replacement buses operate.\nTfL live status (Part Closu
 re\, checked 28 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: Sunday 3 January\, no serv
 ice between West Drayton and Reading. Use GWR services between Maidenhead 
 and Reading. There will also be no GWR services between Paddington and Mai
 denhead\, with some long distance services diverted to/from Euston\, not s
 erving Reading. Replacement buses operate.\nTfL live status (Part Closure
 \, checked 28 November 2026): ELIZABETH LINE: From Sunday 27 December unti
 l Sunday 3 January\, no service between Stratford and Romford. The limited
  services to/from Liverpool Street National Rail station will also not ope
 rate. There will also be no GREATER ANGLIA services between Liverpool Stre
 et and Shenfield. Replacement bus service C operates between Stratford Cit
 y Bus Station (for Stratford and Maryland) and Romford via Forest Gate (Ro
 mford Road)\, Manor Park (Romford Road)\, Ilford\, Seven Kings\, Goodmayes
  (High Road) and Chadwell Heath (Wangey Road). GREATER ANGLIA also operate
  connecting non-stop replacement bus services between Newbury Park (for Ce
 ntral line) and Shenfield / Ingatestone.\n\nSource: TfL planned track clos
 ures\, correct at Monday 16 November 2026. https://tfl.gov.uk/api/document
 /plannedtrackclosures.pdf?id=accc98cf-e761-47b3-a43b-3de08a097b8f&type=doc
 ument\nPlans can change. Check before you travel: https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-
 dlr-overground/status/\nPowered by TfL Open Data\nUnofficial calendar\, no
 t produced or endorsed by Transport for London.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tfl.gov.uk/tube-dlr-overground/status/
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
